cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "dynesty: a dynamic nested sampling package for computing Bayesian posteriors and evidences"
message: >-
  If you use dynesty in your research, please cite both the software
  itself (via the Zenodo DOI below) and the original paper describing
  the method, Speagle (2020), listed under references.
  Please also consider citing the papers describing the underlying
  methods; a tailored list can be generated from the sampler object
  via print(sampler.citations). See
  https://dynesty.readthedocs.io/en/latest/references.html for details.
